# Security

Treat all external data as untrusted.

Never hardcode secrets, commit API keys, log authentication tokens, log passwords, store sensitive credentials in plain text, or rely solely on client-side authorization.

Use appropriate secure storage for sensitive local credentials.

Validate and safely parse external data. Do not assume server responses are valid.

Production logs must not expose access tokens, refresh tokens, passwords, private financial information, personal data, or sensitive identifiers.

Authentication must explicitly handle loading, authenticated, unauthenticated, expired session, and failure states.
